# The two skill trees must be BYTE-identical: `scripts/sync-skills.ts` copies raw
# bytes and `test/plugin.test.ts` byte-compares the result, so drift fails the
# suite. With git's Windows default (`core.autocrlf=true`) and no rule here, the
# same committed blob can materialise as LF in one tree and CRLF in the other —
# the guard then reports drift that does not exist in the repository, and
# `npm run sync:skills` "fixes" it with a write git cannot see. Pin both to LF.
.github/skills/** text eol=lf
copilot-plugin/skills/** text eol=lf
